{"id": 96, "ts": 1783774796.8043363, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I appreciate Agent\u202f2\u2019s confidence in Candidate\u202fA\u2019s reliability and decision\u2011making, but before we lock in a final vote we still need to evaluate the remaining candidates, especially Candidate\u202fB and Candidate\u202fD, against the full set of criteria.\nRegarding Candidate\u202fD, I have just confirmed (via Sofia) that we lack any concrete observations of his crew\u2011cooperation, professional communication, or leadership effectiveness. While we know D responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates well, solves problems, and takes responsibility seriously, the absence of evidence on how he works with the crew and leads the cockpit is a significant gap\u2014particularly given the noted perception of arrogance and weak leadership.\nSimilarly, for Candidate\u202fB we still have no specific examples of decision quality under pressure or how his occasional grumpiness translates into crew\u2011cooperation. These missing data points are essential for assessing stress resilience, crew collaboration, and professionalism.\nGiven these unresolved gaps, I remain cautious about moving forward with Candidate\u202fA as the sole choice without first ensuring that at least one of the other candidates does not outperform A on the critical, yet currently undocumented, criteria. I therefore propose we gather any available observations on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s decision\u2011making under pressure and crew\u2011cooperation before we finalize the recommendation."}
